### InstaPay — fluxo completo (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client)
### Toda escrita exige Idempotency-Key. {{$uuid}} gera uma nova a cada envio;
### para testar replay, fixe um valor e envie duas vezes.

@base = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### 1. Abrir conta da Alice
# @name alice
POST {{base}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "holderName": "Alice Souza", "holderCpf": "529.982.247-25" }

### 2. Abrir conta do Bob
# @name bob
POST {{base}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "holderName": "Bob Lima", "holderCpf": "529.982.247-25" }

### 3. Depositar R$ 100,00 na Alice
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.id}}/deposits
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "amount": "100.00" }

### 4. Transferir R$ 30,25 Alice -> Bob (envie de novo: replay, mesma resposta)
# @name transfer
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-transfer-0001

{
  "debtorAccountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}",
  "creditorAccountId": "{{bob.response.body.id}}",
  "amount": "30.25"
}

### 5. Consultar a transferência
GET {{base}}/transfers/{{transfer.response.body.id}}

### 6. Saldos (derivados do ledger)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.id}}

###
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{bob.response.body.id}}

### 7. Mesma chave, corpo diferente -> 422 idempotency.key_reused
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-transfer-0001

{
  "debtorAccountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}",
  "creditorAccountId": "{{bob.response.body.id}}",
  "amount": "99.00"
}

### 8. Sem fundos -> 422 transfer.insufficient_funds (RFC 7807)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "debtorAccountId": "{{bob.response.body.id}}",
  "creditorAccountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}",
  "amount": "1000.00"
}

### ===================== Chaves de pagamento (Fase 5) =====================

### 9. Registrar chave e-mail na Alice
POST {{base}}/keys
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "accountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}", "type": "EMAIL", "value": "Alice.Souza@Example.com" }

### 10. Registrar chave aleatória (valor gerado pelo servidor)
POST {{base}}/keys
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "accountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}", "type": "RANDOM" }

### 11. Consultar chave (forma canônica: minúsculas) — CPF do titular vem mascarado
GET {{base}}/keys/EMAIL/alice.souza@example.com

### 12. Chaves da conta
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.id}}/keys

### 13. Bob (mesmo CPF da Alice neste exemplo) pede portabilidade da chave -> PORTABILITY
# @name claim
POST {{base}}/key-claims
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "claimerAccountId": "{{bob.response.body.id}}", "keyType": "EMAIL", "keyValue": "alice.souza@example.com" }

### 14. Doadora (Alice) confirma -> chave passa para o Bob
POST {{base}}/key-claims/{{claim.response.body.id}}/confirm
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "accountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}" }

### 15. Excluir chave (só a conta dona)
DELETE {{base}}/keys/EMAIL/alice.souza@example.com?accountId={{bob.response.body.id}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

### ===================== Transferência entre instituições (Fase 6) =====================

### 16. Para outra instituição (ISPB 00000002): 202 PENDING, valor retido; acompanhe pelo GET
# @name external
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "debtorAccountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}",
  "creditor": { "ispb": "00000002", "accountId": "7b0b2f5e-1c1a-4d0e-9a4e-2f1d7f6c9a10" },
  "amount": "10.00"
}

### 17. Status (COMPLETED quando o settlement liquidar)
GET {{base}}/transfers/{{external.response.body.id}}

### 18. Decisão da câmara (settlement-service)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/v1/settlements/{{external.response.body.id}}

### 19. Instituição desconhecida -> settlement rejeita -> compensação (FAILED, saldo devolvido)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "debtorAccountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}",
  "creditor": { "ispb": "99999999", "accountId": "7b0b2f5e-1c1a-4d0e-9a4e-2f1d7f6c9a10" },
  "amount": "5.00"
}

### 20. Para uma chave (resolvida no diretório local)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "debtorAccountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}",
  "creditorKey": { "type": "EMAIL", "value": "alice.souza@example.com" },
  "amount": "1.00"
}

### ===================== Estornos e limites (Fase 7) =====================

### 21. Transferência interna para estornar depois
# @name toRefund
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "debtorAccountId": "{{alice.response.body.id}}", "creditorAccountId": "{{bob.response.body.id}}", "amount": "10.00" }

### 22. Estorno parcial (pago por quem recebeu: Bob -> Alice)
POST {{base}}/transfers/{{toRefund.response.body.id}}/refunds
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "amount": "4.00", "reason": "valor cobrado a mais" }

### 23. Estornos da transferência: total estornado e saldo estornável
GET {{base}}/transfers/{{toRefund.response.body.id}}/refunds

### 24. Limites e uso (spentTonight só aparece entre 20h e 6h, horário de Brasília)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.id}}/limits

### 25. Personalizar limites da conta
PUT {{base}}/accounts/{{alice.response.body.id}}/limits
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{ "perTransaction": "2000.00", "daily": "5000.00", "nightly": "500.00" }
